language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ capital_budget: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A company is considering a number of investments. Each investment will yield a net present value (NPV). Each investment requires a certain cash outflow at the present time. There is a total budget available for investment. How to maximise the NPV obtained from the investments?
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `capital_budget.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/capital_budget.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `capital_budget_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py capital_budget.json
$   savilerow model.eprime capital_budget_1.param -run-solver

$ number of investments, derived from the data: the length of cash_flow (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given cash_flow_dim1 : int(1..)
$ total budget available for investment
given budget : int
$ cash_flow[i]: cash outflow at the present time of investment i, indices 1-based
given cash_flow : matrix indexed by [int(1..cash_flow_dim1)] of int
$ npv[i]: net present value yielded by investment i, indices 1-based
given npv : matrix indexed by [int(1..cash_flow_dim1)] of int

$ x[i]: investment i is chosen
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..cash_flow_dim1)] of bool
$ z: the total net present value of the chosen investments
find z : int(-(sum i : int(1..cash_flow_dim1) . |npv[i]|)..(sum i : int(1..cash_flow_dim1) . |npv[i]|))

maximising z
such that
$ the cash outflows of the chosen investments do not exceed the total budget
(sum i : int(1..cash_flow_dim1) . toInt(x[i]) * cash_flow[i]) <= budget,
$ the total NPV is the sum of the NPVs of the chosen investments
z = (sum i : int(1..cash_flow_dim1) . toInt(x[i]) * npv[i])
